# Keycloak 26.7.0 ships the fixed mssql-jdbc artifact as
# com.microsoft.sqlserver.mssql-jdbc-13.2.1.jre11.jar, but the JAR's embedded
# Maven metadata reports version=13.2.1, so Trivy reports CVE-2025-59250 even
# though the classifier-specific fixed artifact is present. Revisit when
# upstream Keycloak or Trivy normalizes the jre11 classifier.
CVE-2025-59250 exp:2026-08-22

# liblcms2 CVE-2026-41254 (HIGH): the distroless base (gcr.io/distroless/
# java21-debian12) still ships liblcms2-2 2.14-2; Debian fixed it in
# 2.14-2+deb12u1, but distroless lags and has no package manager to patch it in.
# Trivy's DB has flip-flopped on whether it flags this (currently it does not),
# so this is a DEFENSIVE, self-expiring suppression to keep the gate stable if
# it reappears. Low real-world exposure: lcms2 is only reachable via Java AWT/
# ImageIO color-profile handling and Keycloak runs headless. A plain rebuild
# clears it once the base updates. Revisit by the expiry below.
CVE-2026-41254 exp:2026-09-30
